UID:P-DpuDQcl8uFQk6DG68JX
SUMMARY:Houston TCG Con IX
DTSTAMP:20260703T172200Z
DTSTART:20260703T100000Z
DESCRIPTION:Houston TCG Con IX — Your Favorite TCG Weekend in Texas \nThree
	 days. 100+ vendors. Every game that matters. Houston TCG Con IX is back —
	 and the Texas TCG community keeps showing up stronger every round! \nPoké
	mon. Yu-Gi-Oh!. Magic: The Gathering. One Piece. Lorcana. Riftbound. Drago
	n Ball Super. Digimon. Flesh and Blood. If it’s cardboard worth chasing\, 
	it’s on this floor. \n  \n📅 Date: Friday–Sunday\, July 3–5\, 2026 \n⏰ Time
	: Friday: 3PM – 10PM | Saturday: 10AM – 6PM | Sunday: 10AM – 5PM \n📍 Locat
	ion: 9700 Bissonnet St\, Unit 1500\, Houston\, TX 77036 \n🎟️ FREE Entry + F
	REE Parking \n  \n🔥 Event Highlights 🔥 \n🃏 100+ TCG Vendors — Three Days o
	f Cardboard Shop from 100+ vendors traveling from across Texas and beyond.
	 Find singles\, sealed product\, booster boxes\, graded slabs\, Japanese i
	mports\, and rare inserts across every major title — Pokémon\, MTG\, Yu-Gi
	-Oh!\, One Piece\, Lorcana\, Riftbound\, Dragon Ball Super\, Digimon\, Fle
	sh and Blood\, and more. Come with a wantlist. Leave with something you we
	ren’t expecting. \n  \n🤝 The Trade Floor Is Open Bring your binders\, your
	 bulk\, your trade bait\, and your spec pulls. Houston TCG Con is a trade-
	friendly floor — deals happen naturally here because the people at the tab
	les are collectors first. Three days means three days of opportunities to 
	find the trade that makes your collection. \n  \n💸 Deals Across Every Budg
	et From budget bulk and bargain boxes to high-end slabs and competitive si
	ngles — the floor has range. Whether you’re spec buying\, PC hunting\, or 
	just looking to flip smart\, TCG Con IX has the inventory to make it happe
	n. \n  \n💼 Vendor Space Available Table space is open for TCG and collecti
	bles vendors. Come connect with the Texas TCG community. 👉 Apply here: htt
	ps://forms.gle/KFdA1u3pKRAvNtzJ9 \n  \n🏨 Traveling to Houston? Lock In You
	r Rate We’ve secured a special hotel rate exclusively for TCG Con IX atten
	dees. Book your stay and make it a full weekend. 👉 Book here \n  \nThree d
	ays. One floor. The best TCG weekend in Texas. Houston TCG Con IX — July 3
	–5.\n\nhttps://ccs-houston.com/events/houston-tcg-con-ix/\n\nFrom CCS Hous
	ton
URL:https://ccs-houston.com/events/houston-tcg-con-ix/
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:ccs-houston
CATEGORIES:CCS Houston
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT55H
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:fT_HPY9BEoywoz5FO9rTq
SUMMARY:Novel Computational Representations of TCRs and pMHCs Incorporating
	 Structural Information for Translational Applications
DTSTAMP:20260703T172200Z
DTSTART:20260703T140000Z
DESCRIPTION:&#160\;  Speaker: Jared Slone  Doctoral Candidate  Thesis Defen
	se  Department: Computer Science  Location: Duncan Hall 1049  The ability 
	to accurately predict TCR-pHLA binding specificity would have major impact
	s on infectious disease research\, autoimmunity\, and personalized cancer 
	immunotherapy. Experimental characterization of TCR-pHLA binding specifici
	ty is labor-intensive and costly\, however\, and\, despite significant adv
	ances in machine learning\, computationally predicting TCR binding specifi
	city remains difficult. This difficulty arises from both the immense combi
	natorial space of possible TCR-pHLA pairings and the fact that the protein
	s in question possess high degrees of freedom\, making it difficult to mod
	el their physical interactions. This thesis advances the computational cha
	racterization of TCR-pHLA interactions through the development of novel co
	mputational methods for modeling\, representing\, and predicting the behav
	ior of TCR-pHLA pairs.  &#160\;  Central to this thesis is the use of thre
	e-dimensional structural information when predicting TCR-pHLA binding spec
	ificity. First\, this thesis introduces STAG\, a graph convolutional neura
	l network for predicting TCR-pHLA binding specificity from modeled protein
	 structures. STAG incorporates geometric and physicochemical information i
	nto a novel graph representation of TCR-pHLA complexes. The results from t
	his work demonstrate that using holistic structural representations of the
	 proteins as input outperforms prior structure-based approaches for bindin
	g prediction which were based on interprotein contacts.  This thesis next 
	presents STAG-LLM\, a multimodal machine learning architecture that integr
	ates protein language models with structure-based geometric learning. By c
	ombining amino acid sequence-derived embeddings with graph representations
	 of three-dimensional protein structure\, STAG-LLM achieves improved predi
	ctive performance and increased data efficiency compared to approaches tha
	t use sequence or structure alone.  Recognizing that TCR-pHLA interactions
	 are inherently dynamic\, this thesis further introduces STEGG\, a computa
	tional framework for generating structural ensembles of TCR-pHLA complexes
	. Through domain-specific conformational sampling and optimization techniq
	ues\, STEGG efficiently explores the conformational landscape of TCR-pHLA 
	interactions and generates diverse conformational ensembles without the co
	mputational expense of molecular dynamics simulations.  Collectively\, the
	se contributions establish new computational paradigms for computationally
	 representing TCR-pMHC structures\, modeling their flexibility\, and predi
	cting their interactions. More broadly\, this thesis demonstrates advances
	 in structural bioinformatics that improve the computational characterizat
	ion of TCR-pHLA interactions and aid in the development of personalized im
	munotherapies.  (Department : Computer Science)\n\nhttps://events.rice.edu
	/live/events/432802-novel-computational-representations-of-tcrs-and\n\nFro
	m Rice University - Open to the Public
URL:https://events.rice.edu/live/events/432802-novel-computational-represen
	tations-of-tcrs-and
GEO:29.7174;-95.4018
LOCATION:Duncan Hall
X-CALRIPPER-SOURCE:rice-public-events
CATEGORIES:Rice University - Open to the Public
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DURATION:PT1H
END:VEVENT
